                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237967908",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198044970140",
                            "num_reviews": 46,
                            "playtime_forever": 2054,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 2054,
                            "last_played": 1792356307
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For casual play, it's probably okay?, but...\n\n... if you're willing to play it on hardest or near hardest difficulties, do achievements and in-game challenges, then welcome to yet another completely busted so called \"remaster\"! This bug themed digital dumpster filled with enemies you're unable to hit, because everything just goes straight through them, like hitbox and collisions aren't there! Fully invincible enemies, like those last 2 pesky gyrocopters in the chapter where you're controlling big robozilla right before the end of that portion of the level, softlocking you till you happened to restart game from a checkpoint!\n\nOn top of that, there's lots of invisible walls blocking passages you're intended to go and pushing you back once you collide with them. Good example is the section you have to run to the elevator before building collapses. This part is full of these.\n\nAlso if you're going to play around with what game's giving to you - trickshot challanges, then you'll also encounter very janky registering. Often it takes you several tries doing absolutely the same thing, about 10 or sometimes it can jump up to 40+ tries just to make game finally register trickshot you're trying to do this entire time.\n\nBut what's more annoying to me - inaccurate description of what you're suppose to do to complete these.\nSome of them explain exactly what you're suppose to do, others outright mislead you, like challenges with cannonballs.\nIn one challenge it says \"Hit 2 or more enemies with a single cannonball\" and it means exactly that, while the other, very similar challenge says \"Hit 2 or more airborne enemies with a single cannonball\", which in actuality refers to EXPLODING cannonball mid air to kill several airborne enemies. This is especially annoying when you notice that they're exactly specifying difference between direct cannonball hit and cannonball explosion in the same challenge tab. \n\n\nDescription issues probably are around since original release, while the rest is Full Clip Edition related bugs, because I don't remember encountering any of these on initial release.\n\nI gave up on 2 stupidly bugged trickshots called \"Stinger\" and \"Stomach Pump\".\nThey both are absolutely non-functioning, shots are acting like normal instead of charged, for whatever reason charged shots are shot two times one after another consuming both charges, description also is just gibberish and doesn't actually explain what you're suppose to do, kicking drilled enemy at another is completely ignored by the game and they fly where ever but not at the enemy, even doing 180 to auto-aim at a freaking cactus. Yes, I made sure I have disabled both auto-aim options in the settings. \n\nI even out clinical r*tardation of this whole situation decided to count attempts to proc Stinger and it took me 89 attempts... to just finally give up...\n\n*sigh*...\n\n\nYet another example of remasters \"remastering\" original game worse than original game itself.\nI'm sorry, but \"developers\" at this point sounds like mental diagnosis.\nPlease, go see doctors, 'cause this is genuinely feels like insanity. Even I now doubt if I'm still sane after trying out this dog vomit.\n\nAs you can guess, I do NOT recommend it if you're willing to play what this remaster offers you.\nIf you don't care about all it's supposed-to-be-working unique mechanics that made OG game stand out of the rest along side it's comical use of vulgar language and you can't play OG version, then yeah, have fun with this one.",
